
=== 1. non-canonical stored key below a folder (planted via driver), kernel Memory
  list_files('a', recursive=True): OK ['a/ok.txt']
  list_folders('a'): OK []
  get_folder_info('a') (folder_stats push-down): OK [3, 6]
  get_folder_info('') : OK [3, 6]
  sum over list_files('', recursive): OK 2

=== 1b. same, kernel listing-fallback aggregate (driver without folder_stats)
  has folder_stats push-down: False
  get_folder_info('a') (listing fallback): OK [1, 2]

=== 2. non-canonical caller keys: kernel Memory vs Dafny oracle
 [kernel]
  write('d//f'): OK 'd/f'
  exists('d/f'): OK True
  exists('d//f'): OK True
  is_folder('d/'): OK True
  list_files('d'): OK ['d/f']
  write('e/./g'): OK 'e/g'
  is_folder('e/.'): OK True
  list_folders(''): OK ['d', 'e']
  write('h\\i') backslash: InvalidPath path='h\\i' Path contains a backslash | path='h\\i' | backend='memory'
  write('/lead'): InvalidPath path='/lead' Path must not start with '/' | path='/lead' | backend='memory'
  write('p/../q'): InvalidPath path='p/../q' Path contains '..' segment | path='p/../q' | backend='memory'
  read_bytes('./d/f'): OK b'x'
  delete_folder('./'): InvalidPath path='./' Cannot delete the store root | path='./' | backend='memory'
  move src './d/f' -> 'z': OK None
 [oracle]
  write('d//f'): OK 'd/f'
  exists('d/f'): OK False
  exists('d//f'): OK True
  is_folder('d/'): OK True
  list_files('d'): OK []
  write('e/./g'): OK 'e/g'
  is_folder('e/.'): OK True
  list_folders(''): OK ['d', 'e', 'd', 'e']
  write('h\\i') backslash: OK 'h/i'
  write('/lead'): OK 'lead'
  write('p/../q'): InvalidPath path='p/../q' Path contains '..' segment | path='p/../q'
  read_bytes('./d/f'): NotFound path='./d/f'  | path='./d/f' | backend='dafny-oracle'
  delete_folder('./'): NotFound path='./'  | path='./' | backend='dafny-oracle'
  move src './d/f' -> 'z': NotFound path='./d/f'  | path='./d/f' | backend='dafny-oracle'

=== 3. negative max_depth
  [kernel] list_files('x', recursive=True, max_depth=-1): OK []
  [kernel] list_files('x', recursive=True, max_depth=None): OK ['x/a', 'x/y/b']
  [oracle] list_files('x', recursive=True, max_depth=-1): OK ['x/a', 'x/y/b']
  [oracle] list_files('x', recursive=True, max_depth=None): OK ['x/a', 'x/y/b']

=== 4. MOVE/COPY gate vs closed guard on a terminal backend without MOVE/COPY (kernel)
  open, no MOVE: move('s','d'): CapabilityNotSupported path='s' Backend 'memory' cannot move | path='s' | backend='memory' | capability='move'
  open, no COPY: copy('s','d'): CapabilityNotSupported path='s' Backend 'memory' cannot copy | path='s' | backend='memory' | capability='copy'
  closed terminal, no MOVE: move('s','d'): CapabilityNotSupported path='s' Backend 'memory' cannot move | path='s' | backend='memory' | capability='move'
  closed terminal, no COPY: copy('s','d'): CapabilityNotSupported path='s' Backend 'memory' cannot copy | path='s' | backend='memory' | capability='copy'
  closed terminal: exists('s'): BackendUnavailable path=None Backend 'memory' is closed | backend='memory'

=== 5. self-move with spellings differing only by normalisation
  [kernel] move('k/f','k//f'): OK None
  [kernel] exists('k/f') after: OK True
  [kernel] list_files('k'): OK ['k/f']
  [oracle] move('k/f','k//f'): OK None
  [oracle] exists('k/f') after: OK False
  [oracle] list_files('k'): OK []

